    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Blurb.DrunkTier": "Numbers each drink's Endurance roll checks against for each level of drunk. Levels VI–VIII can knock a character out; VII–VIII carry a % chance of death on knockout. To change what each tier does mechanically, use",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Blurb.HungerTier": "% of the character's full satiety pool at which each hunger stage starts. With the defaults, a character who ate a full meal hits Fed at 6 hours, Peckish at 12, Hungry at 18, and Famished at 24. Below zero they drop through four levels of Famished, each one adding 1 point of Hunger Stress and reducing max Stamina by 12.5% (cumulative). Hunger Stress can only be removed by eating.",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Blurb.Intro": "Tune how hunger and drinking work in your game. Saving asks for a world reload. Clear any field to reset it to the recommended value. Hunger doesn't apply to any character until you turn it on for them — click the food icon on the character's sheet and check the box.",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Blurb.SatietyDecay": "How fast a character gets hungry. Every hour they lose (base) + (their BODY divided by the divisor, rounded up) satiety points. The default gives a BODY 7 character 3 satiety lost per hour, so their pool of 72 empties in a day. Combat hunger scales with body size so a huge warrior and a small scholar lose the same PROPORTION of their pool per Stamina spent.",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Chat.SpoilageNotifications": "Announce in chat when food goes bad",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Dialog.Button.Fed": "Fed",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Dialog.Button.Full": "Full",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Dialog.Button.Gorged": "Gorged",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Dialog.Button.Hungry": "Hungry",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Dialog.Button.Peckish": "Peckish",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Hint.CombatSatietyPctPerSta": "How much of the character's satiety pool burns per point of Stamina spent in combat. 0.0025 = 0.25% — a typical character loses about 0.25 satiety per Stamina. Any legacy value above 0.1 is auto-reset to this default (old versions used absolute satiety, new version uses % of pool).",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Section.Chat": "Chat announcements",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Section.ChatHint": "Choose which food events send a message to the chat log. Turning these off doesn't change the game — food still spoils, characters still get sick — you just won't get an announcement when it happens.",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.BaseHour": "Baseline loss per hour",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.BodyDivisor": "BODY divisor (bigger = less loss)",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.CombatSatietyPctPerSta": "Combat drain (fraction of pool per Stamina)",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.Death": "% chance of death on knock-out",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.DefaultDc": "Endurance DC to resist",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.DrunkTierMetadata": "Drunk levels",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.Famished": "Famished",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.FoodDrinkConfiguration": "Food & Drink Configuration",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.HungerTierThresholds": "Hunger stages",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.LevelJump": "Levels gained per failed roll",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.SatietyDecay": "Getting hungry",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.SatietyPerStaSpentCombat": "Combat drain (fraction of pool per Stamina)",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.StatusEffectsEditStatusEffects": "Status Effects → Edit Status Effects",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.Tier": "Level",
    "WITCHER.App.FoodAndDrinkConfig.Text.UnconsciousDc": "Endurance DC to stay conscious",
    "WITCHER.App.GuardConfig.Text.AutoAppliedAtTheStartOfEveryCombat": "Auto-applied at the start of every combat.",
    "WITCHER.App.GuardConfig.Text.ChangePreferredGuard": "Change Preferred Guard",
    "WITCHER.App.GuardConfig.Text.CurrentGuardCanOnlyBeChangedInCombatOutO": "Current guard can only be changed in combat — out of combat it resets to your preferred when the next fight starts.",
    "WITCHER.App.GuardConfig.Text.WardingLocations": "Warding locations (per equipped weapon)",
    "WITCHER.App.HomebrewContentEditor.Blurb": "Enable or disable the bundled homebrew subsystems. House-rule tweaks live in the main settings list; these are added content. Schema is never removed, so turning a system back on is non-destructive. Changes prompt a reload.",
    "WITCHER.App.HomebrewContentEditor.Text.HomebrewContent": "Homebrew Content",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Blurb": "Global tunables for combat mechanics that RAW hard-codes. Per-actor Active Effect overrides still layer on top — these set the world-wide baseline. Consumers read live, so most edits take effect on the next check without a world reload.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.ResetConfirmBody": "Discard all house-rules overrides and restore the shipped defaults? Takes effect when you Save.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.ResetConfirmTitle": "Reset house rules?",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.ResetToDefaults": "Reset to Defaults",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Save": "Save",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Saved": "House rules saved.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.ActionEconomy": "Action Economy",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.AlchemyToxicity": "Alchemy & Toxicity",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.CritWounds": "Critical Wounds",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.DiceRules": "Dice Rules",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.Movement": "Movement",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.Strikes": "Strike Restrictions",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Section.WeaponsDamage": "Weapons & Damage",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.BowsNoStrongDesc": "Removes the Strong Strike option from the attack dialog for bow-type weapons. Crossbows and thrown weapons are already blocked by the shipped code; this folds bows into the same category.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.BowsNoStrongName": "Bows can't make Strong Strikes",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusNeedsSpBreakDesc": "When ON, a critical hit's bonus damage is also suppressed if the base weapon damage failed to break through the target's Stopping Power at the hit location. RAW default: crit bonus bypasses armor and lands regardless. House rule: if the strike itself was fully turned by armor, the crit 'kicker' is turned too.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusBlurb": "Flat bonus damage added on top of the weapon damage roll for each critical wound severity. RAW: normal targets 3 / 5 / 8 / 10; elementa & specter (organ-immune) targets 5 / 10 / 15 / 20. Zero disables that tier's bonus.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusComplex": "Complex bonus",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusDeadly": "Deadly bonus",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusDifficult": "Difficult bonus",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusNeedsSpBreakName": "Crit bonus damage needs SP break",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusNoOrgansHeading": "Organ-immune targets (elementa, specter)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusNormalHeading": "Normal targets",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBonusSimple": "Simple bonus",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBracketComplex": "Complex (beat by)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBracketDeadly": "Deadly (beat by)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBracketDifficult": "Difficult (beat by)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBracketSimple": "Simple (beat by)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritBracketsBlurb": "Attack-vs-defense delta required to score each critical wound severity. RAW: 7 / 10 / 13 / 15. Values are auto-sorted on save so simple < complex < difficult < deadly always holds.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritSpDowngradeDesc": "If the incoming damage didn't break through the target's Stopping Power at the hit location, downgrade the rolled critical wound severity. Off = RAW behavior. Greater→Lesser = Difficult/Deadly wounds drop one tier. Any→Simple = every crit that fails to pierce lands as Simple regardless of the rolled tier.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritSpDowngradeMode": "Downgrade critical wound when damage doesn't pierce SP",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritSpModeAnyToSimple": "Downgrade Any to Simple",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritSpModeGreaterToLesser": "Downgrade Greater to Lesser",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.CritSpModeOff": "Off (RAW)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.D10CollapseDesc": "When ON (RAW default), a natural 1 fires the fumble table AND rolls another d10 that subtracts from the total, chaining on further 10s. When OFF, a natural 1 still fires the fumble table but the drain die is skipped — no additional negative chain.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.D10CollapseName": "d10 rolls collapse on a natural 1 (bad day)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.D10ExplodeDesc": "When ON (RAW default), a natural 10 on any skill / check / attack roll triggers another d10 that adds to the total, repeating on further 10s. When OFF, a 10 is just a 10 — no bonus chain.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.D10ExplodeName": "d10 rolls explode on a natural 10 (kickass)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ExtraActionStaCost": "Extra Action STA cost",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ExtraActionStaCostDesc": "Flat STA drain applied at round-tally time when an Extra Action fires (RAW: 3).",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ExtraActionToHit": "Extra Action to-hit penalty",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ExtraActionToHitDesc": "To-hit penalty on any shot flagged as an Extra Action — the second shot of a Fast attack, second Joint shot, caster action after weapon action, etc. (RAW: -3.)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ExtraDefenseStaCost": "Extra Defense STA cost (per defense after the first)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ExtraDefenseStaCostDesc": "Cumulative STA drained per defense after the free first one in the round (RAW: 1). Set to 0 to disable the cumulative cost entirely.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.NewSilverRulesDesc": "R. Talsorian 7/11/25 rule update. ON: weapons get a Silver Weapon Trait checkbox — trait-tagged weapons deal full damage to silver-weak monsters and half to everyone else. The legacy \"silver\" weapon quality is hidden and disabled (no isSilver stamp, no separate silver damage roll). OFF: the trait is inert (hidden UI, no effect) and the legacy silver quality behaves as it always did.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.NewSilverRulesName": "New Silver Rules (RTG 7/11/25)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.OffhandPenalty": "Off-hand attack penalty",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.OffhandPenaltyDesc": "Base penalty for off-hand weapon attacks (RAW: -3). Applies to Joint Attack's second shot, ambidextrous swaps, and any weapon flagged as off-hand. Per-actor reductions still fold on top.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.RawToxicityDesc": "When ON (RAW, Core p.248), combined potion / decoction toxicity above your cap inflicts the Overdosed status — a poison-style DoT that lasts until toxicity drops back to cap or a DC 18 Endurance check purges the last potion. When OFF, toxicity is still tracked on the sheet but never harms you.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.RawToxicityName": "RAW toxicity overdose",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.SplitMovementDesc": "When ON, movement can be split across the turn and interleaved with actions up to total SPD. When OFF (RAW), all movement must be taken before any action — acting forfeits remaining movement for the round.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.SplitMovementName": "Split movement across actions",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ProneCrawlDesc": "House rule (not RAW): a prone actor may crawl instead of the RAW \"stand first, then move.\" A normal move caps at SPD/5 and a full-turn Run at three times that (both rounded down, minimum 1 — so a running crawl always covers at least ~2m). Running is allowed. When OFF (default), prone imposes no movement cap.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.ProneCrawlName": "Prone crawl (move = ⅕ SPD)",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.StrongStrikePenalty": "Strong Strike to-hit penalty",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Text.StrongStrikePenaltyDesc": "Base penalty applied to Strong Strike attack rolls (RAW: -3). Per-actor reductions (perks / feats) still fold on top.",
    "WITCHER.App.HouseRulesConfig.Title": "House Rules",
    "WITCHER.App.OpenCategoryConfigDialog.Label.DamageDice": "Damage dice",
