    "WITCHER.Brawl.Action": "Brawl Action",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Block": "Block",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Charge": "Charge",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Choke": "Choke",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Drag": "Drag",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteDrag": "Usable by EITHER party in a grapple. A Physique vs Physique test (auto-rolled — the target does NOT defend with a combat skill). On a win, pick a reachable location and drag the foe (and yourself, still holding each other) there. Distance = the difference between your Physique bases, minimum 2m, capped by your remaining movement.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DragNeedsTokens": "Drag needs both you and the target on the canvas.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DragNoMovement": "No movement left this turn to drag anyone.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DragNeedsGrapple": "Drag requires an active grapple on the target.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DragWhilePinned": "You can't drag while a pin locks you in place — break the pin first.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DragPickDest": "Click a highlighted tile to drag there — right-click or Esc to cancel.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DragPickFacing": "Pick which side to twist the foe to — e.g. against a wall (right-click / Esc to keep their side).",
    "WITCHER.CombatExtended.Action.Drag": "Drag",
    "WITCHER.CombatExtended.Action.DragDesc": "Usable by EITHER party in a grapple. An opposed Physique test (auto-rolled) — the target does NOT defend with a combat skill. On a win, pick a reachable tile and drag the foe (and yourself, still holding each other) there. Distance = the difference between your Physique bases, minimum 2m, capped by your remaining movement.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeNeedsPin": "Choke can only be used on a foe you have PINNED first.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeNeedsGrapple": "Choke can only be used on a foe you're grappling.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeMaintainPrompt": "Keep choking — spend which action?",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeNormal": "Normal action (×1 damage)",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeExtra": "Extra action (×2 damage)",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeLoc": "Throat",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ChokeAlready": "You're already choking {name} — it's maintained on your turn.",
    "WITCHER.Doc.BrawlMixin.Text.ChokeContinues": "{name} keeps choking — {dmg} suffocation (stamina, then HP).",
    "WITCHER.Mech.Choke.UpkeepTitle": "Choke — keep it up?",
    "WITCHER.Mech.Choke.UpkeepBody": "Keep choking <strong>{name}</strong>? Takes your WHOLE turn (a full-round action) and deals <strong>{dmg}</strong> suffocation (stamina, then HP).",
    "WITCHER.Mech.Choke.UpkeepKeep": "Keep choking (full round)",
    "WITCHER.Mech.Choke.UpkeepRelease": "Release",
    "WITCHER.Mech.Choke.NoAction": "Can't maintain the choke — it takes your whole turn, and you've already acted.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DefenseTotal": "Total to defend",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.DialogTitle": "Brawl",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Disarm": "Grapple Disarm",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Escape": "Escape",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Grapple": "Grapple",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.GroupDefense": "Defense",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.GroupGrapple": "Grapple / Wrestling",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.GroupSpecial": "Special",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.GroupStrikes": "Strikes",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Kick": "Kick",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NonLethal": "Bludgeoning · non-lethal",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteBlock": "Block a melee attack with your limbs — a Brawling defense roll. A defensive reaction (no action needed), so it stays available even with no actions left. Only blocks attacks you could plausibly stop bare-handed.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteCharge": "Full round: move up to your Run speed, then make a strong strike (-3 to hit). If the attack is blocked, make a Physique check vs the target's Physique to knock them prone.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteChoke": "Only on a foe you have PINNED. A hold: deals 3 + melee bonus suffocation THROUGH armor (plus any Strangling-weapon bonus), each turn you maintain it. Maintain by re-Choking every turn — spend a normal action (×1) or the extra action (×2 damage); an un-maintained choke releases on your next turn. Done with Brawling or a Strangling weapon (not plain grappling). Resisted with Brawling (or a Grappling weapon) — no dodge/escape.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteChokeRaw": "Requires a grapple. Roll Brawling vs the foe's Brawling. The target is suffocating — a flat 3 damage each turn — until they escape (Dodge/Escape vs your Brawling).",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteDisarm": "Made at −4; you must be in a grapple. Roll Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) vs the foe's Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) or Dodge/Escape. On a success: PUNCH damage to their weapon arm, and the weapon is knocked 1d6m in a random direction — or make a DC 18 Brawling check to snatch it for yourself instead.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteDisarmRaw": "You must be in a grapple. Roll Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) vs the foe's Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) or Dodge/Escape. On a success: PUNCH damage to their weapon arm, and the weapon is knocked 1d6m in a random direction.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteEscape": "You are held (grappled, pinned, clinched, or choke-held). Roll Dodge/Escape vs each holder's Brawling. Each hold you beat is cleared; ones you don't beat, you stay in.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteGrapple": "Roll Brawling vs the target's Dodge/Escape. While grappled they cannot move away and take -2 to all physical actions. Prerequisite for pins, chokes and throws; each turn the target may roll Dodge/Escape vs your Brawling to slip loose.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteKick": "Kick: REF + Brawling to hit, dealing your Kick damage as non-lethal (bludgeoning). May be a strong or fast strike.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NotePin": "Requires a grapple. On a success the target is immobilized and cannot move or act until they escape (Dodge/Escape vs your Brawling).",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NotePunch": "Punch: REF + Brawling to hit, dealing your Punch damage as non-lethal (bludgeoning). May be a strong or fast strike.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NotePush": "Requires you to be grappling the target. Roll Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) vs Brawling or Dodge/Escape. No damage. On a success, push the target a number of metres equal to your Physique base (BODY + Physique) ÷ 5, rounded down, in a direction you choose — snapping them to the nearest grid cell and breaking any grapple or pin they're in. If they're shoved into a wall, they take 1d6/2 ramming damage per 2m travelled (torso, bypassing armour but not a magic shield).",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NotePushKick": "Instead of dealing full damage you may push the target back a number of metres equal to your Body/3. This attack does half damage and always hits the torso. If they're shoved into a wall, they take 1d6 ramming damage (torso, bypassing armour but not a magic shield).",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteReleaseGrapple": "Voluntarily let go of every hold you currently maintain (grapple, pin, chokehold, mount). No roll required. Both parties are free to move again.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteReverseGrapple": "You are grappled (but not pinned or choked). Roll Brawling opposed by your grappler's Brawling — on a win, dominance swaps and they're the one grappled now.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteThrow": "Requires a grapple. The target is thrown to the ground (prone), takes damage equal to your Punch damage, and must make a Stun save at -1.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteTrip": "Grappler only. Like Takedown — roll Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) vs the foe's Brawling. On a success, deal NON-LETHAL punch damage (to Stamina — still reduced by SP, only ramming ignores armour) and the TARGET falls prone. You stay on your feet and keep the grapple hold.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteTripRaw": "Grappler only. Roll Brawling vs the foe's Brawling. On a success the target is knocked prone (no damage). You stay on your feet.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.TripTargetProne": "You can't trip a target that's already prone.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Pin": "Pin",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Punch": "Punch",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Push": "Push",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Slam": "Slam",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Takedown": "Takedown",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.TackleNeedsTarget": "Tackle needs a target — pick the foe you're smashing into.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.TakedownSelfProne": "You must be standing to take someone down — get up first.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.TakedownTargetProne": "You can't take down a target that's already prone.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.PinNeedsProneOrWall": "You can only pin a foe that's prone or backed against a wall.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteTakedown": "Usable while grappling OR being grappled. Roll Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) vs the foe's Brawling. On a success, deal NON-LETHAL punch damage (to Stamina — still reduced by SP, only ramming ignores armour) and BOTH of you go prone while keeping the grapple hold.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.SlamPickDirection": "Click where to slam the target (right-click or Esc to cancel).",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.SlamProne": "You can't slam while prone — get up first.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.PushTargetProne": "You can't push a prone target — there's nothing to shove back.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.NoteSlam": "Requires an active grapple. Roll Brawling (or a Grappling weapon's skill) vs Brawling or Dodge/Escape. On a success, deal DOUBLE kick damage (non-lethal, to Stamina — still soaked by SP) to a random location, knock the target prone, throw them a fifth of your Physique base (BODY + Physique) metres, rounded down, in a direction you choose (breaking the grapple), and force a Stun save. The impact deals an additional 1d6 ramming damage to the target's torso, bypassing armour (but not a magic shield); if slammed into a wall, add 1d6/2 more per 2m travelled.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.PushKick": "Push Kick",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ReleaseGrapple": "Release Grapple",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.ReverseGrapple": "Reverse Grapple",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.RollButton": "Roll Brawl",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.StatusApplied": "Applied {status} to {targets}.",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.StatusManual": "On a hit, apply {status} (no target selected).",
    "WITCHER.Brawl.Throw": "Throw",
