    "WITCHER.Roll.Fumble": "Fumble! (natural 1 — roll on the fumble table)",
    "WITCHER.Roll.FumbleWarning": "Fumble! Natural 1 — resolve it on the fumble table.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AdrenalineEnabled.Hint": "Use the Core optional Adrenaline rule (p.175-176): bank a d6 per critical hit (pool capped at BODY), then spend dice for +1d6 damage or +1d6 temporary HP, paying Stamina per die. Turn this OFF to remove adrenaline from character sheets, the chrome UI, the combat dock, and weapon attack dialogs entirely. Requires reload.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AdrenalineEnabled.Name": "Adrenaline (optional rule)",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AdrenalineStaPerDie.Hint": "Stamina spent for each adrenaline die committed to damage or temp HP. Core RAW is 10 (p.176). Only used when the Adrenaline optional rule is on.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AdrenalineStaPerDie.Name": "Stamina per adrenaline die",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AutoSceneDarkness.Hint": "Let the inbuilt clock drive the viewed scene's darkness — bright at midday, dark at night, ramping across dawn and dusk, with storms and fog dimming the daytime. GM only; ignored when 'Inbuilt time & weather' is off.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AutoSceneDarkness.Name": "Auto scene darkness",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AutoWeatherFx.Hint": "Draw the current weather (rain, snow, hail, sandstorm, fog, clouds, lightning) on the scene canvas. GM only; ignored when 'Inbuilt time & weather' is off.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.AutoWeatherFx.Name": "Auto weather effects",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CarouselInitiativeConfig.MenuHint": "Configure the horizontal initiative carousel that appears under the top bar during combat: enable, audience/context gates, layout, motion, disposition colors, and privacy filters.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CarouselInitiativeConfig.MenuLabel": "Configure Carousel Initiative",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CarouselInitiativeConfig.MenuName": "Carousel Initiative",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CombatTileTargeting.Name": "Canvas tile-targeting in combat",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CombatTileTargeting.Hint": "Click a weapon in the combat dock to paint its range on the canvas, then click a tile to attack the token on it (ranged/thrown show the range band on hover). Disables canvas middle-click token targeting while on — the combat-tracker rightbar keeps target/untarget as a fallback. Turn off to attack immediately using the old targeting.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CriticalWoundsPack.Hint": "The Item compendium the critical-wound roller draws from. Wounds are matched by location, severity, and lesser/greater variant, so any compendium with critical-wound items works.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CriticalWoundsPack.Name": "Critical Wounds Compendium",
    "WITCHER.Settings.CriticalWoundsPack.None": "— None —",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.alchemyPotency.Hint": "Expanded alchemy rules. Components and mutagens carry a potency value; the sum across a brew's ingredients sets the output tier (Normal / Enhanced / Superior). Oils stick to weapons for 24 hours and consume a charge per damaging hit. Toxicity ticks HP damage. Adds new formulae (White Gull, Zerrikanian Powder) and witcher potions (Trance, Stammelford's Philter, Wolverine, White Honey). Turn off for pure RAW.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.alchemyPotency.Name": "Homebrew: Alchemy Reborn",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.bookSystem.Hint": "Enables the 3-type book system (monster lore, skill, stress) on valuable items. Disable for RAW Witcher TRPG.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.bookSystem.Name": "Homebrew: Book System",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.dicePokerTable.Hint": "Enables the Witcher dice poker table — a GM-opened betting dice game (up to 4 seats, real dice items, currency stakes). Disable for RAW Witcher TRPG.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.dicePokerTable.Name": "Homebrew: Dice Poker Table",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.extendedCombat.Hint": "Enables the optional combat overhaul: guard stances (Balanced / Warding / Closed / Fool's), Raise Shield, revised attack / defense costs and effects, and a GM-tunable Combat Actions editor. Based on The Duderonomist's Equipment Overhaul and rule adaptations. Disable for RAW Witcher TRPG.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.extendedCombat.Name": "Homebrew: Combat Extended",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.farkleTable.Hint": "Enables the Farkle gambling table — a GM-opened betting dice game (up to 4 seats, real dice items, currency stakes). Disable for RAW Witcher TRPG.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.farkleTable.Name": "Homebrew: Farkle Table",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.foodAndDrink.Hint": "Enables food/drink charges and the drunkenness track (Sober Up). Disable for RAW Witcher TRPG.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.foodAndDrink.Name": "Homebrew: Food & Drink",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.merchant.Hint": "Enables the merchant actor: shops with dynamic pricing and buy/sell flow, plus scene merchant cards. Disable to remove merchant features.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.merchant.Name": "Merchant",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.rawToxicity.Hint": "When ON (RAW, Core p.248), going over your toxicity cap inflicts the Overdosed condition (3 damage/turn, ignores armor) until your toxicity drops back to the cap or you pass a DC 18 Endurance check (1 action), which purges the last potion you drank. When OFF, toxicity is still tracked but never harms you — leave it off for a house rule.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.rawToxicity.Name": "RAW Toxicity Overdose Rules",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.splitMovement.Hint": "When ON, movement can be split across your turn and interleaved with actions, up to your total SPD (e.g. SPD 8: move 3, act, move 2, extra action, move 3). When OFF (RAW), all movement must be taken at the start of your turn before any action — once you act, you forfeit any remaining movement.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.splitMovement.Name": "House Rule: Split Movement",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.stress.Hint": "Adds a stress counter to characters, with stress books to release it.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.stress.Name": "Homebrew: Stress Mechanic",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.witcherReborn.Hint": "Replaces the RAW witcher-school bonuses with six per-school training packs (Cat / Wolf / Bear / Griffin / Viper / Manticore). Each school has four passive perks, a skill bonus, and a heroic action. The Witchers Reborn compendium contains the race items; drop the appropriate school on a Witcher character to grant its perks. When OFF, only RAW witcher school data is used.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.Homebrew.witcherReborn.Name": "Homebrew: Witchers Reborn",
    "WITCHER.Settings.HouseRulesConfig.MenuHint": "Global tunables for combat mechanics: strike restrictions, crit downgrade, action-economy costs, strong-strike and off-hand penalties.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.HouseRulesConfig.MenuLabel": "Configure House Rules",
    "WITCHER.Settings.HouseRulesConfig.MenuName": "House Rules",
    "WITCHER.Settings.SceneDefaults.Created": "Created the Default Scene Template. Adjust its settings and close — new scenes will inherit them.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.SceneDefaults.MenuHint": "Opens a hidden template scene in the normal scene configuration. Whatever you set here (token vision, lighting, grid, environment…) is copied onto every new blank scene you create. It is a default, not a global override — existing scenes are never changed.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.SceneDefaults.MenuLabel": "Edit Template",
    "WITCHER.Settings.SceneDefaults.MenuName": "Default Scene Settings",
    "WITCHER.Settings.SceneDefaults.TemplateName": "Default Scene Template",
    "WITCHER.Settings.ShowWelcome.Hint": "Show a short welcome + support message the next time this world loads. Also toggleable via the checkbox on the dialog itself.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.ShowWelcome.Name": "Show welcome message on load",
    "WITCHER.Settings.StealthConfig.MenuHint": "Turn the whole stealth subsystem on/off and tune every knob it uses: range-band modifiers, base sight distance, cross-level detection, chat verbosity, cone rendering behavior.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.StealthConfig.MenuLabel": "Configure Stealth",
    "WITCHER.Settings.StealthConfig.MenuName": "Token Stealth",
    "WITCHER.Settings.TimeFlowRate.Hint": "In-world seconds that pass per real second while the game is unpaused, so the clock runs on its own. 1 = real time (the default). Raise it for a faster narrative clock — e.g. 60 = one in-world minute per real second (a full day in 24 real minutes). Set to 0 to freeze the clock and move time only by hand or in combat. The GM drives it and it stays synced for everyone; pausing stops it.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.TimeFlowRate.Name": "Clock speed (running time)",
    "WITCHER.Settings.UiCustomizer.MenuName": "UI Customizer",
    "WITCHER.Settings.UiCustomizer.MenuLabel": "Customize UI",
    "WITCHER.Settings.UiCustomizer.MenuHint": "Recolour the interface, assign fonts to headers / body / mono text, and add custom CSS. The GM sets a world default; each player can add a personal override on top.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherBiome.Hint": "The regional climate that drives the inbuilt weather engine. Temperate is the default Continent lowland; Highland is colder and windier; Coastal is wet and stormy; Arid is hot and dry.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherBiome.Name": "Weather climate",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherDebug.Hint": "Show a numeric intensity badge (e.g. \"[cloud 2 · snow 1 · wind 0]\") next to weather labels in the Time & Weather console, so you can see which tier each layer is running at. GM aid; per-client; never shown to players.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherDebug.Name": "Weather debug badge",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherEnabled.Hint": "Show the system's own date/time/weather widget and calendar. Turn this OFF to use an external calendar or weather module instead — combat round timers, oil/coating countdowns, and status-effect durations keep working either way, since they run on Foundry's world time. Requires reload.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherEnabled.Name": "Inbuilt time & weather",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherMaxParticles.Hint": "Maximum number of weather particles drawn at once. Lower this if weather effects stutter on your machine. Per-client.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherMaxParticles.Name": "Weather particle budget",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherSound.Hint": "Let the GM drive a 'Weather' playlist whose looping stems (rain, hail, wind, blizzard) follow the current weather. Plays for everyone — adjust loudness with the Environment volume slider in the Playlists sidebar.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherSound.Name": "Weather ambience",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherThunder.Hint": "Play thunderclaps during lightning storms. Per-client; mute it here without affecting other players.",
    "WITCHER.Settings.WeatherThunder.Name": "Thunder",
    "WITCHER.Setup.AlchemyConsts.Dialog.Button.Bad": "Bad",
    "WITCHER.Setup.AlchemyConsts.Dialog.Button.Good": "Good",
    "WITCHER.Setup.AlchemyConsts.Dialog.Button.Great": "Great",
    "WITCHER.Setup.AlchemyConsts.Dialog.Button.Neutral": "Neutral",
    "WITCHER.Setup.AlchemyConsts.Dialog.Button.Optimal": "Optimal",
    "WITCHER.Setup.AlchemyConsts.Dialog.Button.Weak": "Weak",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Handlebars.Text.NumberA": "Number(a)",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Dialog.Button.ConfigureFoodDrink": "Configure Food & Drink",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Dialog.Button.ConfigureStress": "Configure Stress",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Dialog.Button.ConfigureBooks": "Configure Books",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.BookConfiguration": "Book System Configuration",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.BookConfig": "Tune the in-world reading cooldowns for the book system — how long between monster-lore / skill study sessions and between novel chapters. Language requirements and study difficulty are configured per book.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Dialog.Button.EditQualities": "Edit Qualities",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Dialog.Button.EditStatusEffects": "Edit Status Effects",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Dialog.Button.ManageHomebrewContent": "Manage Homebrew Content",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.FoodAndDrinkConfig": "Edit how fast satiety decays per hour, at what satiety values each hunger tier kicks in, and the per-tier metadata (Endurance DC, level jump, unconscious / death thresholds) the drunk roll uses.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.HomebrewContent": "Enable or disable the bundled homebrew subsystems — book system, stress, food & drink, the Farkle and Dice Poker tables, and the merchant. House-rule tweaks stay in the main settings list.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.ImmersiveTokenCamera": "GM-only global toggle. When ON, every client locks their view to their controlled token — always centered, facing always up. Zoom still works; pan is disabled. Auto-releases when nothing is selected or multiple tokens are selected.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.ImmersiveTokenCameraShowHint": "When ON, a small tooltip above the dock lists the two immersive-camera keybindings (Esc = deselect token, Shift+A/D = rotate token) while a token is selected. Client-scoped — each player can hide it independently.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.QualitiesEditor": "Edit the catalog of weapon and armor qualities. Defaults seed from the Core Rulebook effect names; you can add, edit, or remove entries.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.RotationCostsMovement": "How much of your per-turn movement budget is spent for every 90° of token rotation in combat. Sub-90° rotations accumulate. Default 0 (rotation is free). Set to a positive number to charge for spinning in place.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.SpdUnitsPerPoint": "How many of the scene's grid-distance units equal one point of SPD when canvas drags charge the movement budget. Default 1 (Witcher RAW: 1 SPD = 1 metre, scene grid in metres). Use 3 for scene-grid-in-feet with 1 SPD ≈ 1 metre, or 5 for hex-board convention (1 SPD = 5 ft).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.StatusEffectsEditor": "Customize what each combat status does — damage-over-time, stat and roll penalties, action locks, ending checks — or add and remove statuses. Defaults are strict Core Rulebook RAW.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Hint.StressConfig": "Toggle the recovery penalty on/off, tune the WILL-save threshold multiplier and post-save clear target, set the breakdown-cap-before-handover, and adjust the stress granted by each critical wound severity. Boon / break tables and stress-shield dice live in the Status Effects editor.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.FoodDrinkConfiguration": "Food & Drink Configuration",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.HomebrewContent": "Homebrew Content",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.ImmersiveTokenCamera": "Immersive Token Camera",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.ImmersiveTokenCameraShowHint": "Immersive Token Camera — Show Control Hint",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.RotationCostsMovementMetersPer90": "Rotation costs movement — meters per 90°",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.SceneUnitsPerSPDPoint": "Scene units per SPD point",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.StatusEffects": "Status Effects",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.StressConfiguration": "Stress Configuration",
    "WITCHER.Setup.Settings.Text.WeaponArmorQualities": "Weapon & Armor Qualities",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Chat.GiftGave": "<div class=\"wdm-gift-card\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-gift\"></i> <strong>{sender}</strong> gave <strong>{item}</strong> to <strong>{target}</strong>.</div>",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Chat.GiftGaveQty": "<div class=\"wdm-gift-card\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-gift\"></i> <strong>{sender}</strong> gave <strong>{item}{qty}</strong> to <strong>{target}</strong>.</div>",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Chat.ShieldAbsorbs": "<div class=\"wdm-attack-rider\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-shield-halved\"></i> <strong>{label}</strong> — {target}'s active shield absorbs the {status} effect.</div>",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Chat.TookCoin": "<div class=\"wdm-gift-card\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-coins\"></i> <strong>{sender}</strong> took <strong>{move} {coin}{plural}</strong> from <strong>{source}</strong>.</div>",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Chat.TookEverything": "<div class=\"wdm-gift-card\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-hand-holding-dollar\"></i> <strong>{sender}</strong> took everything from <strong>{source}</strong>.</div>",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Dialog.Button.BodyBlock": "Body Block",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Dialog.Button.Reposition": "Reposition",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Dialog.Button.ResistMagic": "Resist Magic",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Notify.GiftFailedOnXInternalId": "Gift failed on {target}: internal id missing on new item (see console).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Notify.GiftFailedOnXXSee": "Gift failed on {target}: {val0} (see console).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Notify.GiftLinkContentsFailed": "Gift to {target}: '{item}' failed to link contents (see console).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Notify.GiftPartialCreated": "Gift partial-created {created}/{total} items on {target} — aborting so the giver's copy isn't lost.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Notify.GiftWrongContents": "Gift to {target}: '{item}' saved with wrong contents (see console).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Text.AppliedTo": "Applied to",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Text.CastShield": "Cast shield",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Text.CoinPlural": "s",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Text.MagicShieldStoppedCrit": "{shield} stopped critical wound",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Text.MagicShieldSoaked": "{shield} soaked {n}",
    "WITCHER.Setup.SocketHook.Text.MagicShieldShattered": "{shield} shattered",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.Dialog.Button.PurgeOverdose": "Purge Overdose",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.Dialog.Button.PutOutFire": "Put Out Fire",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.Dialog.Button.Stand": "Stand",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.Dialog.Button.WashOffAcid": "Wash Off Acid",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.acid.Description": "4 damage at the start of each turn — eats through armor (ignores SP). Spend an action to wash it off, or escape the source.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.aim.Description": "Aim N: a full-round action grants +1 to your next ranged attack, stacking to +3 over consecutive rounds. Applied automatically and cleared when you fire.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.bleed.Description": "2 damage at the start of each turn — armor does NOT soak it. A Healing spell or a DC 15 First Aid check (1 action) stops it.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.blinded.Description": "−3 to all attack and defense, −5 to sight-based Awareness. Spend an action to clear your eyes.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.burning.Description": "5 damage to every body location each turn (armor soaks the hit) and the flames eat 1 SP off the armor covering each location. Spend an action to put it out (pour water / stop-drop-roll).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.charging.Description": "Charging — next attack is locked to Strong Strike (RAW: -3 to hit, ×2 damage). If the attack is blocked, roll Physique vs the defender's Physique to knock them prone.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.dead.Description": "Slain.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.diseased.Description": "−2 to every action and maximum Stamina cut by a quarter while ill. Periodic Endurance checks stave off nausea. Only a Doctor's treatment (a Healing Hands check) plus a full night's rest clears it.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.drunk-3.StressNote": " Loosens the chest: clears 1 STRESS on apply.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.drunk-4.StressNote": " Clears 1 STRESS on apply.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.drunk-5.StressNote": " Clears 1 STRESS on apply.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.drunk-6.StressNote": " Clears 1 STRESS on apply.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.entangled.Description": "Wrapped up: −5 SPD and −2 to all physical actions. On your turn, a DC 18 Dodge/Escape or Contortionist check breaks free; an ally may spend an action to remove it.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.exhausted.Description": "−1 to every roll until you rest.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-1.Description": "Very Hungry — −12.5% max STA.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-1.StressNote": " +1 Hunger Stress from this depth — only cleared by eating.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-2.Description": "Weakening — −25% max STA.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-2.StressNote": " +2 Hunger Stress from this depth — only cleared by eating.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-3.Description": "Famished — −37.5% max STA, −1 all rolls.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-3.StressNote": " +3 Hunger Stress from this depth — only cleared by eating.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-4.Description": "Starving — −50% max STA, −2 all rolls. Collapse below −MAX.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished-4.StressNote": " +4 Hunger Stress from this depth — only cleared by eating.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished.Description": "Starving. −50% max STA, −2 to every roll.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.famished.StressNote": " Hunger Stress is granted by the hunger cascade.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.fastDraw.Description": "You snap-drew a weapon and MUST make an attack with it this turn (RAW Core p.165). Roll into initiative at +3 and take −3 on that attack. If the turn ends without attacking, the snap-draw is wasted and Fast Draw clears with a chat warning. Cleared automatically when the attack lands.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.fed.Description": "Fed — comfortable. No mechanical effect.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.freeze.Description": "−3 SPD and −1 REF. A DC 16 Physique check (1 action) breaks the ice.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.full.Description": "Full — well-fed. No mechanical effect.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.gorged.Description": "Gorged — overfull. −1 REF, −1 DEX (sluggish). The full belly powers daily recovery — counts as +2 REC for healing purposes (your displayed REC stat is unchanged).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.gorged.StressNote": " The heavy meal clears 2 STRESS on apply.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.grappled.Description": "Held in a grapple: −2 to all physical actions and you can't move away. Use the Escape action (Dodge/Escape vs the grappler's Brawling) to slip free. If not also pinned or choked, you may Reverse Grapple (opposed Brawling) to swap dominance.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.hallucinating.Description": "GM-controlled false sensory images. A DC 15 Deduction check recognizes each illusion for what it is.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.hangover.Description": "Hangover — paying for last night. Your head's pounding, your stomach's a knot, and every REC roll feels like climbing out of a well. Sleep it off over the next few days.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.hungry.Description": "Hungry — no stat debuff yet.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.hungry.StressNote": " +1 Hunger Stress on descent — only cleared by eating back past Peckish.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.intoxicated.Description": "−2 REF / DEX / INT and −3 Verbal Combat; 25% chance you won't remember what you did.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.isChoking.Description": "Applying a chokehold: the target takes 3 + your melee damage bonus in suffocation damage each turn you maintain it. (CE only.)",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.isGrappling.Description": "Grappling someone: you cannot move away without releasing the grapple. Under Combat Extended, you also take −2 to all physical actions except against the actor(s) you hold.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.isMounted.Description": "Riding a larger enemy: you cannot move independently — you move wherever they move. You are in their blind spot; they must spend a Move + Brawling check vs your Ride to attack you. (CE only.)",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.isPinning.Description": "Pinning someone: −3 to all physical actions except against the pinned foe; you cannot move away until you release the pin. (CE only.)",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.mounted.Description": "A rider clings to your back — they're in your blind spot. To attack them, you must spend a Move and beat their Ride check with Brawling. (CE only.)",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.nausea.Description": "Every 3 rounds, roll under BODY or spend the round vomiting and dry-heaving.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.overdosed.Description": "Toxicity over your limit (Core p.248): 3 damage at the start of each turn — armor does NOT soak it. It lifts the moment your toxicity falls back to your cap. You may also use the Action menu (1 action) to make a DC 18 Endurance check that purges the last potion you drank.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.paralyzed.Description": "Cannot act or defend; a helpless target is hit on a roll of 10+.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.peckish.Description": "Peckish — getting hungry. No mechanical effect yet, but Hungry is one tick away.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.pinned.Description": "Pinned after a successful grapple: immobilized — you cannot move or act. Attacks against you land on a roll of 10+. Escape with a Dodge/Escape roll opposed by the grappler's Brawling.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.poisoned.Description": "3 damage at the start of each turn — armor does NOT soak it. A DC 15 Endurance check (1 action) ends it.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.prone.Description": "Knocked down: −2 to attack and defense until you spend an action to stand.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.restrained.Description": "Movement is blocked. Break free with an Athletics or Brawling check.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.restrictedVision.Description": "Vision restricted (visor down or shield covering your head): −2 to Block, Parry, and Dodge until your next turn or the obstruction is removed.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.staggered.Description": "−2 to attack and defense; recovers automatically at the start of your next turn.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.stunned.Description": "You can take no actions and cannot defend; attacks land on a roll of 10+. At the start of your turn make a Stun save to end it — being struck while stunned also snaps you out.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.suffocation.Description": "3 damage at the start of each turn — armor does NOT soak it. Ends the moment air is restored (surfacing, escaping a chokehold).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.unconscious.Description": "Out cold: treated as stunned — no actions, no defense, auto-hit. Wakes at 20+ STA with a passed Stun save.",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusClauses.yrden.Description": "Trapped in Yrden's circle — REF and SPD penalties scale with the STA the caster poured into the sign (errata: -1 at 1 STA, -2 at 3 STA, -3 at 5 STA, -4 at 7 STA).",
    "WITCHER.Setup.StatusEffects.Dialog.Button.AimX": "Aim {n}",
